WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.075
Welcome to Grade 4 English, Unit
1: Daily Life & Communication.

2
00:00:04.155 --> 00:00:11.264
In Unit 1 you explore daily life and communication:
what people do every day, and how they share their ideas.

3
00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:17.134
You read about routines, letters and mail,
steady effort and fairness, and you meet Amal,

4
00:00:17.214 --> 00:00:20.102
who interviews Omar at the town post counter.

5
00:00:20.182 --> 00:00:27.489
You learn verb patterns, adverbs with the present simple,
have got, Wh- questions, imperatives and conjunctions,

6
00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:29.468
using the twenty Unit 1 words.

7
00:00:29.548 --> 00:00:35.799
By the end you can interview someone about their
work and write a fair, clear report about them.

8
00:00:35.879 --> 00:00:41.340
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:49.534
By the end of this unit, you will be able to talk and write
about your daily routine and the things you do every day.

10
00:00:49.614 --> 00:00:56.677
You will also explain why communication, including
letters, mail and language, matters to a community.

11
00:00:56.757 --> 00:01:02.910
You will also use verb patterns correctly,
for example agrees to send and enjoys playing.

12
00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:05.501
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:05.581 --> 00:01:11.069
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
mail, language, citizen, agree, continue, gain.

14
00:01:11.149 --> 00:01:15.919
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:15.999 --> 00:01:19.691
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:19.771 --> 00:01:24.285
The reading sequence includes A Day at
the Post Counter and My Daily Routine.

17
00:01:24.365 --> 00:01:25.120
Read actively.

18
00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.236
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:29.316 --> 00:01:33.114
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:33.194 --> 00:01:35.992
The first language focus is Verb Patterns.

21
00:01:36.072 --> 00:01:40.720
A verb pattern is the way we join
a verb to the word that follows it.

22
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.723
Some verbs take to and another verb,
and some take a verb ending in -ing.

23
00:01:45.803 --> 00:01:49.423
Choosing the right pattern keeps your sentences clear.

24
00:01:49.503 --> 00:01:56.892
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

25
00:01:56.972 --> 00:02:01.168
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Describe Your Daily Routine.

26
00:02:01.248 --> 00:02:05.203
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

27
00:02:05.283 --> 00:02:08.274
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

28
00:02:08.354 --> 00:02:11.466
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

29
00:02:11.546 --> 00:02:12.972
You are ready to begin.

30
00:02:13.052 --> 00:02:19.458
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

31
00:02:19.538 --> 00:02:22.603
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

32
00:02:22.683 --> 00:02:29.874
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
